<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    COMPACT PASS HEAD (§4.6, §4.6 rules) - Block A only, 64dp, for secondary screens
    (detail, forms, scanner, discover). Keeps the tear line as the bottom edge so a detail page
    still reads as part of the same credential system.

        20dp gutter  paddingTop, under the status-bar inset - the same 20dp screen gutter
                      the full pass head shows below the inset
        20dp row     eyebrow (overline, on_primary_muted)  +  one optional trailing slot
        44dp row     title (headline 28/34, on_primary, max 1 line)  +  optional count
        1dp          divider_perforation_dark

    The result count belongs on the title row, baseline-aligned with the title, so it reads as
    part of the title line instead of floating above the title's cap height in the eyebrow row.
    The 20dp eyebrow row is too short to hold a second text line for that job.

    The title always keeps the row's remaining width (0dp + weight 1), so a long count can never
    push it below the majority of the line: the count is capped at ui_pass_head_count_max (~40% of
    the row at the narrowest supported width). Inside that cap it autosizes from the overline size
    (11sp) down to ui_pass_head_count_text_min (9sp), so a longer label steps down instead of
    losing its end; ellipsis only applies if even 9sp does not fit.

    The label is bounded first at the data layer: every screen renders it through
    CountLabel.format, which compacts the number (28 EVENTS, 1.2K EVENTS, 12K EVENTS, 1.2M EVENTS)
    and never exceeds 16 characters. The autosize above is the safety net for a long translation,
    not the fix for a long count.

    Usage: the same contract as include_pass_head.xml, through PassHeadBinder.bindCompact().

        <include android:id="@+id/passHead" layout="@layout/include_pass_head_compact"
                 android:layout_width="match_parent" android:layout_height="wrap_content" />

    ids: passHead, passHeadIdentity (inset this one), passHeadEyebrow, passHeadTitle,
         passHeadTitleCount (overline count, made visible by setting its text),
         passHeadTrailing (a slot in the eyebrow row - an icon button, or a short action label;
         metadata and result counts belong on the title row, never here),
         passHeadTear.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/passHead"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:orientation="vertical">

    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/passHeadIdentity"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:background="@drawable/bg_pass_head"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/ui_gutter"
        android:paddingTop="@dimen/ui_gutter"
        android:paddingEnd="@dimen/ui_gutter">

        <LinearLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/ui_pass_head_compact_row"
            android:gravity="center_vertical"
            android:orientation="horizontal">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/passHeadEyebrow"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.EventQR.Type.Eyebrow"
                android:textColor="@color/ui_on_primary_muted"
                tools:text="Discover" />

            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/passHeadTrailing"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="match_parent"
                android:gravity="center_vertical|end"
                android:orientation="horizontal" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/passHeadTitleRow"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:baselineAligned="true"
            android:orientation="horizontal">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/passHeadTitle"
                android:layout_width="0dp"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_weight="1"
                android:minHeight="@dimen/ui_pass_head_title_min"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.EventQR.Type.Headline"
                android:textColor="@color/ui_on_primary"
                tools:text="Scan" />

            <!-- Baseline-aligned to the title by the row. GONE until a screen sets a count, so a
                 head without one keeps the title's full width. Capped so the title keeps the
                 majority of the row; inside the cap the text steps down from the overline size to
                 9sp, so a longer count shrinks rather than truncates. The text itself comes from
                 CountLabel.format (<= 16 characters), so autosize stays a safety net. Autosize is
                 set here on the one shared include, not per screen and not on the shared
                 TextAppearance (the appearance is used by eyebrows, tabs and labels that must not
                 shrink). -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/passHeadTitleCount"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/space_12"
                android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="@dimen/ui_type_overline"
                android:autoSizeMinTextSize="@dimen/ui_pass_head_count_text_min"
                android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
                android:ellipsize="end"
                android:maxLines="1"
                android:maxWidth="@dimen/ui_pass_head_count_max"
                android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.EventQR.Type.Eyebrow"
                android:textColor="@color/ui_on_primary_muted"
                android:visibility="gone"
                tools:text="28 EVENTS"
                tools:visibility="visible" />
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- The tear line sits ON the dark block, so the 24%-white dashes are visible and the
             block still ends on a hard edge. -->
        <View
            android:id="@+id/passHeadTear"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/stroke_hairline"
            android:background="@drawable/divider_perforation_dark"
            android:importantForAccessibility="no" />
    </LinearLayout>

</LinearLayout>
